    "body": "Is it my imagination, or is the use of this function redundant? Instead of doing all combinations of two dimensions, why not just do all three dims at the same time? Or one dimension at a time?\r\n\r\n```\r\nfunc rectIntersect(i1, i2 *Item, x, y Axis) bool {\r\n\td1 := i1.GetDimension()\r\n\td2 := i2.GetDimension()\r\n\r\n\tcx1 := i1.Position[x] + d1[x]/2\r\n\tcy1 := i1.Position[y] + d1[y]/2\r\n\tcx2 := i2.Position[x] + d2[x]/2\r\n\tcy2 := i2.Position[y] + d2[y]/2\r\n\r\n\tix := math.Max(cx1, cx2) - math.Min(cx1, cx2)\r\n\tiy := math.Max(cy1, cy2) - math.Min(cy1, cy2)\r\n\r\n\treturn ix < (d1[x]+d2[x])/2 && iy < (d1[y]+d2[y])/2\r\n}\r\n```",
    "closed_by": null,
